# Node / TS
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
.npm/
.pnpm-store/
# ⛔ `package-lock.json` IS NOT IGNORED, AND IT WAS — IN A GENERIC "Node / TS" BLOCK.
#
# That is the boilerplate pattern for a LIBRARY. ProductOS ships a Dockerfile that does
# `COPY package.json package-lock.json ./` followed by `npm ci`, and `npm ci` refuses to run
# without a lockfile. So:
#
#   - the image could not be built from a commit at all. A fresh clone has no lockfile, the COPY
#     fails, and the build dies. It worked only on machines that happened to have one locally.
#   - the Dockerfile's own stated invariant — "the image is a pure function of the lockfile" — was
#     unenforceable, because the lockfile was not in the commit the image claims to be a function of.
#   - a git worktree could not `npm install` or run the suite, which is how this was found: the
#     deploy checkout had no lockfile and no node_modules, and `npm run build` appeared to work only
#     because node walked up to the main checkout's modules.
#
# ⛔ `yarn.lock` and `pnpm-lock.yaml` STAY IGNORED. This project is npm; one of those appearing is a
# mistake, not a second opinion.
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml

